    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the others are helper/base classes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership-level tenure rule in `OwnerMapper.toMembershipLevel`:\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for zero namesakes) are now capped at 3, and level 4 is granted only when tenure exceeds 365 days, computed as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`. Since a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is set to today (zero tenure), a new owner never exceeds level 3 \u2014 a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` of 0 lands exactly at level 3.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `membershipLevel` schema description and raised `maximum` from 3 to 4 to match the new range and rule.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` (asserting a new owner with email caps at level 3, not 4) passes, and the build is green.",
